WEBVTT

00:00.270 --> 00:05.250
<b>This is a work of fiction. The names of the people, places, and organizations
are fictitious and in no way related to any real person or entity.</b>

00:14.110 --> 00:15.360
<i>It's so peaceful.</i>

00:16.530 --> 00:19.610
<i>I hope these days continue forever.</i>

00:20.530 --> 00:22.570
<i>Anyway, back to class.</i>

00:31.140 --> 00:34.650
<i>Well, that peace sure didn't last.</i>

02:15.820 --> 02:18.080
<i>The hell is that?! A nose bubble?</i>

02:18.080 --> 02:19.820
<i>No, an antler bubble?!</i>

02:25.570 --> 02:27.410
<i>A fairytale scene... but only visually!</i>

02:32.470 --> 02:34.360
<i>Why do you sound like that in your sleep?</i>

02:34.360 --> 02:39.220
<i>Or rather, don't fall asleep during class. 
Especially this boldly.</i>

02:44.220 --> 02:50.130
<i>As the class rep, student council president, 
and this deer's caretaker,</i>

02:50.130 --> 02:51.310
<i>I should probably wake her up.</i>

02:52.020 --> 02:54.440
Hey, Shikanoko. Wake up.

02:56.900 --> 02:58.070
<i>And she's not waking up.</i>

02:58.410 --> 03:01.660
Shikanoko! Hey, Shikanoko!

03:01.660 --> 03:02.410
Wake—

03:05.220 --> 03:06.280
<i>Wha?</i>

03:06.630 --> 03:10.160
<i>Reflexes so sharp, you wonder 
if she's really asleep at all.</i>

03:19.200 --> 03:21.380
Is she rowing a boat now?

03:21.670 --> 03:27.320
Well, I mean, I can understand 
getting sleepy during last period.

03:28.080 --> 03:28.770
Huh?

03:31.390 --> 03:32.520
A bird?!

03:33.370 --> 03:34.900
Followed by more!

03:37.350 --> 03:39.150
<i>And she hasn't noticed at all!</i>

03:39.670 --> 03:41.150
<b>10 Minutes Later</b>

03:39.770 --> 03:41.150
<i>Ten minutes later.</i>

03:43.460 --> 03:45.340
Okay, wake up already!

03:45.340 --> 03:47.490
Koshi-san? What's the matter?

03:47.490 --> 03:48.970
Er, it's nothing.

03:49.850 --> 03:53.580
<i>Some things have to be called out, 
even in the middle of class.</i>

03:54.080 --> 03:57.450
And then an adjective gets added here...

03:59.360 --> 04:01.380
<i>It's a little late to be asking now, but...</i>

04:01.850 --> 04:05.890
<i>Why is no one saying a damn thing 
about all of this?!</i>

04:05.890 --> 04:09.260
Jab, jab. Jab, jab.

04:07.550 --> 04:10.270
<i>Just </i>My Deer Friend Nokotan<i> Things.</i>

04:10.500 --> 04:13.890
<i>She's seriously not waking up at all. 
It's messed up!</i>

04:14.120 --> 04:17.350
Let's see... Who should we have 
translate this sentence into Japanese?

04:17.350 --> 04:22.920
Well, today's the 12th, so the person 
who's attendance number 12!

04:23.820 --> 04:24.700
<i>Crap!</i>

04:24.050 --> 04:24.110
<b>Number 12</b>

04:24.360 --> 04:24.700
<b>Number 12</b>

04:24.990 --> 04:26.160
Hey, Shikanoko!

04:26.300 --> 04:31.180
<b>Psssssszzzzzzzzz</b>

04:29.980 --> 04:31.550
She's gonna call on you!

04:33.170 --> 04:35.790
Let's see. Number 12 is...

04:36.090 --> 04:37.330
Shikanoko!

04:44.570 --> 04:46.840
Your tag's still on.

04:49.060 --> 04:52.450
No way! Oh, no! I forgot to cut the tag off!

04:52.450 --> 04:55.200
Wait, my tag's not still on, is it?!

04:55.200 --> 04:57.170
Hey, who was that just now?

05:00.380 --> 05:02.060
<i>And she's still asleep!</i>

05:02.060 --> 05:04.450
<i>Could you not say such 
stress-inducing things in your sleep?!</i>

05:04.720 --> 05:09.020
<i>You can bet Class 3-B didn't 
get any work done after that.</i>

05:10.450 --> 05:13.950
<b>Hokkaido
Notsuke Peninsula
Shiretoko Mountain Range</b>

05:13.950 --> 05:17.460
<b>Hokkaido
Notsuke Peninsula
Mount Rausu</b>

05:24.470 --> 05:26.840
<b>MY DEER FRIEND NOKOTAN</b>

05:27.850 --> 05:30.470
Well, well...

05:33.040 --> 05:35.350
I definitely smell something.

05:45.850 --> 05:48.330
This pressure... It couldn't be.

05:48.330 --> 05:50.620
All right. Time for club.

05:50.860 --> 05:52.740
Hey, Shikanoko. Let's go.

05:53.400 --> 05:56.780
Huh? She was just here a moment ago.

06:07.750 --> 06:09.180
Who're you?!

06:10.140 --> 06:13.630
The scent was coming from here, 
but I guess it got away.

06:13.630 --> 06:15.520
You're from a whole other world!

06:15.980 --> 06:20.210
I, Kumatori Soichiro, was once known 
as a legendary Matagi hunter,

06:20.210 --> 06:22.200
but it seems I've lost my edge.

06:22.200 --> 06:24.160
My life's greatest regret.

06:24.160 --> 06:26.410
Uh... You just randomly 
started recounting your past?

06:26.410 --> 06:28.900
But thanks. At least I know who you are now.

06:29.180 --> 06:31.580
<i>But why'd a Matagi suddenly show up?</i>

06:31.580 --> 06:34.280
<i>Not to mention, this dude 
is definitely trespassing.</i>

06:37.910 --> 06:42.660
Um... What could a Matagi want at our school?

06:42.660 --> 06:44.920
Did you get permission to be here?

06:46.830 --> 06:48.170
It's still warm.

06:48.440 --> 06:51.380
This dude's not listening to me at all.

06:51.380 --> 06:53.250
My quarry can't have gone far.

06:53.250 --> 06:55.110
No, really! Did you get 
permission to be here—

06:55.110 --> 06:56.170
I won't let you escape!

07:02.180 --> 07:03.940
Guess I'm reporting him.

07:03.940 --> 07:05.120
Is he gone?

07:05.120 --> 07:08.860
Huh? Shikanoko? Hey, where are you?

07:09.690 --> 07:10.450
Huh?

07:10.790 --> 07:13.120
Whew, I'm saved.

07:13.120 --> 07:14.830
This <i>is</i> a school, right?!

07:14.830 --> 07:16.970
What's goin' on with our floors?!

07:16.970 --> 07:20.700
Thank goodness I made some modifications 
just in case something like this happened!

07:20.700 --> 07:23.420
Don't go modifying school property!

07:23.420 --> 07:25.460
Want me to report you, too?

07:25.460 --> 07:30.230
More importantly, what's 
that Matagi even doing here?

07:30.230 --> 07:32.470
He was touching your desk.

07:32.470 --> 07:35.100
Today's the Day of the Deer.

07:35.100 --> 07:36.260
The Day of the Deer?

07:36.490 --> 07:38.080
<i>The Day of the Deer,</i>

07:39.760 --> 07:42.320
<i>on the fourth Tuesday 
of each month in Hokkaido,</i>

07:42.320 --> 07:46.970
<i>was introduced in order to promote the 
consumption of Yezo deer meat to the masses.</i>

07:47.660 --> 07:49.550
That's very specific to Hokkaido!

07:49.550 --> 07:52.290
Don't try to apply local rules to Hino!

07:52.290 --> 07:54.200
No wonder I've never heard of it!

07:54.500 --> 08:00.450
Wait a minute. Does that mean that Matagi 
came here to capture you, Shikanoko?

08:00.450 --> 08:05.100
That's right. And he's super persistent, too.

08:05.100 --> 08:06.590
You actually know the guy?!

08:06.890 --> 08:08.840
If he catches me, it'll all be over!

08:08.840 --> 08:12.340
A gibier festival will be held 
in front of Hino Station,

08:12.560 --> 08:16.150
and the citizens of Hino will 
make a delicious meal of me!

08:16.150 --> 08:18.560
Gibier! Gibier!

08:18.560 --> 08:23.480
Spare a thought for the Hino citizens 
who just wanted to use the train.

08:23.480 --> 08:26.850
Anyway, I gotta spend today 
running away from him!

08:26.850 --> 08:29.610
Huh? Wait, where are you going?! Hello?

08:29.610 --> 08:31.610
<b>RUNNING BEGINS</b>

08:30.020 --> 08:31.610
<i>And the running begins.</i>

08:47.850 --> 08:50.130
I smell its scent nearby.

08:50.350 --> 08:51.320
<i>Gulp.</i>

08:58.440 --> 09:00.140
There's no use in hiding!

09:09.020 --> 09:11.450
Tch. I mistook my prey for another.

09:15.000 --> 09:17.160
Huh? What the?!

09:15.000 --> 09:17.160
<b>Clueless Yet Again
Nekoyamada Neko-san (3rd-Year)</b>

09:23.470 --> 09:25.160
I've found you!

09:48.940 --> 09:50.010
Must be this way.

09:50.580 --> 09:52.910
Whoa, what the heck?

09:53.830 --> 09:56.780
There's some weird old dude over there.

09:56.780 --> 09:59.060
For real. Hilarious.

09:58.760 --> 10:00.700
<b>UNEXPECTED VISITORS</b>

09:59.060 --> 10:00.700
<i>The irregularly occurring gyaru!</i>

10:01.870 --> 10:04.160
Hey, mister. Whatcha doin'?

10:04.160 --> 10:06.460
Like, what are you doing? Cosplay?

10:06.840 --> 10:08.960
No... Er, I, uh...

10:08.960 --> 10:13.110
OMG, did you hear him? 
He legit talks like a grandpa!

10:13.110 --> 10:16.030
Take a picture with us! 
Let's put it up on Insta!

10:16.030 --> 10:17.380
"Insta"?

10:17.380 --> 10:19.910
Er... I don't know what you're talking about.

10:19.910 --> 10:22.720
C'mon!

10:23.690 --> 10:26.080
Okay, look at my phone!

10:27.170 --> 10:28.970
<i>He's chasing you, isn't he?</i>

10:28.970 --> 10:30.480
<i>This is your chance to run!</i>

10:30.480 --> 10:32.360
Gyaru!

10:32.360 --> 10:35.020
<i>Thus we prove the existence 
of deer-friendly gyaru.</i>

10:35.020 --> 10:36.820
<i>Q.E.D.</i>

10:36.820 --> 10:38.320
<b>RUN</b>

10:37.050 --> 10:38.320
<i>Run.</i>

10:39.840 --> 10:41.070
<b>RUN</b>

10:40.000 --> 10:41.070
<i>Run!</i>

10:42.570 --> 10:43.580
<i>Run!</i>

10:42.570 --> 10:43.580
<b>RUN</b>

10:45.650 --> 10:48.460
<i>Nokotan's epic escape continued.</i>

10:48.460 --> 10:50.210
<b>THE PURSUER</b>

10:49.060 --> 10:50.210
<i>The pursuer...</i>

11:03.600 --> 11:05.600
<b>THE PURSUED</b>

11:04.250 --> 11:05.600
<i>and the pursued.</i>

11:05.600 --> 11:07.100
<b>Principal's Office</b>

11:08.100 --> 11:10.640
<b>Every Miller Draws Water to His Own Mill</b>

11:49.020 --> 11:52.520
<b>Every Miller Draws Water to His Own Mill</b>

12:04.650 --> 12:09.330
<i>The fierce battle continued 
even after midnight.</i>

12:09.600 --> 12:11.910
<i>"But the Day of the Deer 
is over now, isn't it?"</i>

12:12.230 --> 12:14.710
<i>No basic jokes like that here.</i>

12:29.360 --> 12:30.180
<i>Take that.</i>

12:32.290 --> 12:33.720
<i>Steppy, steppy, steppy, step.</i>

12:43.350 --> 12:46.700
<i>This was a battle with everything on the line.</i>

13:09.490 --> 13:14.140
Seems I've finally tracked you down, Noko-san.

13:15.640 --> 13:18.150
<b>NOKOTAN'S IN DIRE STRAITS</b>

13:15.990 --> 13:18.150
<i>Nokotan's in dire straits!</i>

13:19.470 --> 13:20.520
Shikanoko!

13:20.870 --> 13:22.440
You guys are still at it?!

13:22.440 --> 13:23.570
Koshitan!

13:24.570 --> 13:27.410
Witness how our battle ends!

13:27.630 --> 13:28.530
Huh?

13:28.840 --> 13:29.930
I...

13:31.370 --> 13:36.640
I will never fall to you! 
Bring it, Kumatori Soichiro!

13:47.300 --> 13:49.800
The hell is that weapon?! 
It looks super inconvenient to use!

13:52.200 --> 13:53.850
And what is this mystery dimension?!

13:53.850 --> 13:57.100
Oho... At least you're a lively one.

13:57.100 --> 14:01.480
But you won't be talking like that for long...

14:02.100 --> 14:04.280
Shikanoko Noko!

14:10.800 --> 14:12.800
<b>This is my rifle.</b>

14:14.930 --> 14:19.430
<b>There are many like it, but this one is mine.</b>

14:19.690 --> 14:24.440
<b>My rifle is my best friend. It is my life.</b>

14:26.280 --> 14:28.440
<b>I must master it as</b>

14:28.440 --> 14:30.780
<b>I must master my life.</b>

14:32.450 --> 14:33.580
<b>My rifle</b>

14:33.580 --> 14:37.750
<b>and myself are the defenders of my country.</b>

14:38.290 --> 14:41.650
<b>We are the masters of our enemy.</b>

14:41.920 --> 14:45.300
<b>We are the saviors of my life.</b>

14:52.950 --> 14:54.450
Your life is mine!

14:54.450 --> 14:56.830
Shikanoko!

14:59.070 --> 15:01.000
Oh, time out for a sec.

15:04.540 --> 15:05.850
H-Hello—

15:05.850 --> 15:08.340
<i>Hey! Where the hell are you?!</i>

15:08.340 --> 15:10.680
<i>Hurry up and buy the daikon radish 
I asked for and head home!</i>

15:10.680 --> 15:12.340
Darlin', I'm sorry—

15:12.340 --> 15:13.820
<i>Where are you right now?!</i>

15:13.820 --> 15:15.120
I'm in Hino right now...

15:15.120 --> 15:17.670
<i>Where the hell's Hino?! In Douou?!</i>

15:17.670 --> 15:21.350
No, uh... Tokyo.

15:21.350 --> 15:25.340
<i>What?! There ain't no Hino in the 23 wards!</i>

15:25.340 --> 15:28.700
There's a place called 
the Tama region in Tokyo.

15:28.700 --> 15:31.360
I'll buy some Nerima daikon and head home.

15:31.360 --> 15:34.730
<i>How many hours do you think it'll take you 
to get from Nerima to Nemuro, huh?!</i>

15:36.770 --> 15:38.750
Did... Did he go home?

15:39.870 --> 15:43.580
This is what friendship, effort, 
and victory look like!

15:41.020 --> 15:47.380
<b>Friendship</b>

15:41.890 --> 15:47.380
<b>Effort</b>

15:42.640 --> 15:47.380
<b>Victory</b>

15:43.580 --> 15:45.690
Yeah, I don't think you'll be 
standing shoulder-to-shoulder

15:45.690 --> 15:47.380
with a Jump protag anytime soon.

15:47.630 --> 15:51.140
All right! I'm gonna win the next 
Day of the Deer, too!

15:51.140 --> 15:52.550
He's gonna be coming by every month?!

15:53.330 --> 15:57.810
<i>The thought of every fourth Tuesday awaiting 
her plunged Koshitan into a deep despair.</i>

15:59.100 --> 16:00.990
What's that on your shoulder?

16:00.990 --> 16:02.440
Huh? Oh!

16:02.440 --> 16:05.140
I-I'm sort of in a hurry...

16:05.140 --> 16:06.700
You'll be coming to the station with us.

16:06.700 --> 16:09.340
Hey, this is a real gun!

16:09.340 --> 16:10.320
What?!

16:10.320 --> 16:19.200
<b></b>When carrying or transporting a firearm,



said firearm must be placed in a container.

16:10.320 --> 16:19.200
<b></b>(Excerpt from the Firearm and Sword Possession Control Law)

16:10.960 --> 16:19.200
<i>When carrying or transporting a firearm, 
said firearm must be placed in a container.</i>

16:22.860 --> 16:26.670
<i>Something tells me we won't be 
seeing him next Day of the Deer.</i>

16:27.710 --> 16:30.710
<b>Hokkaido
Nemuro Strait
Stream</b>

16:48.980 --> 16:53.240
<b>Deer
Crackers</b>

16:49.400 --> 16:51.110
<i>One hour ago.</i>

16:49.500 --> 16:51.110
<b>One Hour Ago</b>

16:51.110 --> 16:53.240
Let's do our best in the 
Deer Club again today!

16:53.240 --> 16:55.280
Why are you wearing a tracksuit?

16:55.280 --> 16:58.240
Oh, I just sent my uniform to the cleaners.

17:03.370 --> 17:05.200
It's all ripped.

17:06.120 --> 17:07.750
Look, over there, too.

17:06.120 --> 17:12.210
<b>Deer
Crackers</b>

17:08.290 --> 17:09.480
And there.

17:10.320 --> 17:12.030
And the knees!

17:12.820 --> 17:15.450
They sure get tattered quickly 
when you go walking.

17:15.450 --> 17:18.340
Walking? Or hiking on game trails?!

17:20.310 --> 17:27.400
<b>Deer
Crackers</b>

17:25.080 --> 17:27.400
It may be spring, but it's still chilly.

17:27.630 --> 17:30.990
Sometimes, reality just hits you.

17:32.330 --> 17:35.150
Fine. Let's go buy you a new tracksuit.

17:35.150 --> 17:38.620
Yay! Shopping!

17:40.370 --> 17:43.050
Is it really so exciting?

17:45.920 --> 17:47.370
Koshitan!

17:47.690 --> 17:49.030
Yeah!

17:49.930 --> 17:51.000
By the way...

17:51.000 --> 17:52.960
Where are we?

17:52.960 --> 17:54.170
Hino!

17:54.170 --> 17:56.760
I know that much, you dumbass!

17:57.100 --> 17:59.050
We were supposed to go straight to the store,

17:59.050 --> 18:02.410
but we got lost because 
you kept making stops!

18:02.410 --> 18:08.150
But... But I kept seeing really 
cool sticks to pick up...

18:09.030 --> 18:10.900
What are you, a grade schooler?!

18:11.570 --> 18:12.550
Oh, damn it!

18:12.550 --> 18:15.900
I've done this for 11 episodes, and I still 
don't know a damn thing about Hino!

18:16.550 --> 18:19.940
Okay. If we go down that hill, 
we'll be in the shopping district.

18:20.490 --> 18:21.850
Come on, let's go.

18:21.850 --> 18:23.540
Er, huh?

18:24.470 --> 18:25.480
Shikanoko?

18:25.480 --> 18:26.400
Where'd you...

18:29.930 --> 18:31.370
What are you doing?

18:32.140 --> 18:33.520
Plastic bottles.

18:33.520 --> 18:34.520
Huh?

18:34.520 --> 18:36.130
Plastic bottles.

18:37.460 --> 18:39.870
Ah, right. You're scared of them.

18:39.870 --> 18:42.070
I guess that was a plot point somewhere.

18:47.430 --> 18:49.610
Um... Shikanoko?

18:50.780 --> 18:52.330
There's some behind you, too.

18:57.320 --> 18:58.820
<i>This is still Nokotan.</i>

18:57.460 --> 18:58.820
<b>NB: Nokotan</b>

19:01.570 --> 19:03.720
Just how scared are you?

19:19.610 --> 19:22.250
C-Come on. Stand up already.

19:22.250 --> 19:24.630
We don't really have a choice, 
so we're taking another way.

19:24.630 --> 19:26.680
I-I'm the president, remember?

19:26.680 --> 19:29.690
It's the president's job to take 
care of the deer, or something.

19:30.030 --> 19:32.850
Damn it, you sure are a handful, though.

19:42.890 --> 19:45.870
<i>Damn it... Whenever I'm with her...</i>

19:46.350 --> 19:47.380
<i>I always...</i>

19:48.100 --> 19:49.230
<i>always...</i>

19:51.610 --> 19:53.090
<i>get thrown off balance.</i>

19:54.470 --> 19:55.720
Is something wrong?

19:56.430 --> 19:58.090
No, it's nothing!

19:58.090 --> 19:59.960
Ah, Koshitan!

20:08.390 --> 20:10.120
We're back where we started.

20:10.980 --> 20:13.220
Hino is just cursed!

20:13.220 --> 20:17.740
There are plastic bottles around every corner!

20:18.480 --> 20:21.890
How did you even survive this long?

20:30.650 --> 20:32.550
Ooh!

20:33.440 --> 20:35.550
That should take care of things for now.

20:35.550 --> 20:38.750
Well, wearing a tracksuit won't 
be against the rules, at least.

20:38.980 --> 20:41.260
That's a surprising skill.

20:41.570 --> 20:43.650
A former delinquent who's good at sewing...

20:43.650 --> 20:46.260
It's more common than you'd think, 
but that's why it's good!

20:46.260 --> 20:48.890
You want me to literally zip your mouth shut?

20:49.170 --> 20:52.020
Thanks, Koshitan! I'll treasure it!

20:52.020 --> 20:55.880
Sure. I-If it gets ripped again, 
I'll sew it up for you.

20:55.880 --> 20:57.440
Yay!

20:57.580 --> 20:58.290
<b>Rip</b>

20:59.120 --> 21:01.690
My butt just ripped.

21:03.320 --> 21:04.970
Come here already.

21:04.970 --> 21:05.960
Okay!

21:06.320 --> 21:09.550
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

21:06.960 --> 21:10.010
<i>She's a pain in the ass... 
but this isn't so bad.</i>

21:10.870 --> 21:13.510
<i>I hope these days continue forever.</i>

22:47.370 --> 22:49.980
Koshi-san, good morning.

22:49.980 --> 22:50.930
Good morning.

23:01.370 --> 23:04.020
This part and this part will be on the test!

23:04.300 --> 23:06.780
And this part might not be.

23:14.240 --> 23:15.660
Heya.

23:15.660 --> 23:17.530
You're late, Onee-chan.

23:17.530 --> 23:20.320
Koshitan-senpai, you're late.

23:20.320 --> 23:23.330
Well, Shikanoko's been missing all morning.

23:23.760 --> 23:25.840
Have you guys seen her?

23:26.410 --> 23:27.590
Onee-chan?

23:28.970 --> 23:32.220
Who's Shikanoko?

23:32.970 --> 23:33.650
Huh?
